+# GOAL — block 18: menus — neighbour-generated supports under the unsoldered reading, cube orbits under the soldered one (2026-09-15)
+
+**Owner directive (2026-09-15):** don't stop; assess the next lane at each conclusion; no subagents; derivations over computation.
+
+**Why this block.** The derivation campaign's verdict table (#8093) has one row left *to compute*: "Menus — neighbour-generated supports (menus-and-Born block) — clause candidate: none if derived". Its Born half ("which overlap functions are consistent with order-blindness") is closed by PR #8137 (order-blindness forces the invariant kernel). The support half is open: which subsets of the sphere can carry the records, given the recorded neighbours, under each reading of the possibility-covariance sentence.
+
+**Object.** The rule's conditional `r(· | positions and values of the recorded neighbours)` on the pure-state sphere `S²`; its support. Two readings: *unsoldered* — the internal rotations `SO(3)` act on values independently of the lattice group on positions, and the rule is covariant under both; *soldered* — one copy of the cube's rotation group `O` (24 proper rotations) acts on values and positions together.
+
+**Contract.**
+- M1 (unsoldered, one recorded neighbour of value `q`): the support is invariant under the rotations about `q`; a finite invariant set lies in `{q, −q}` (every other point has an infinite orbit). With no recorded neighbour the invariant law is uniform (the landed possibility-covariance note; restated). Two or more recorded neighbours whose values are all `±q` reduce to this case.
+- M2 (unsoldered, two non-collinear recorded values): the stabilizer is trivial; the supports are exactly the frame-attached assignments `S(q_1, q_2) = F(q_1, q_2) · S_0(q_1·q_2)` with `F` the equivariant frame and `S_0` an arbitrary subset per angle; no finite site-independent menu is covariant.
+- M3 (soldered): a site-independent finite menu is covariant iff it is a union of `O`-orbits on `S²`; the orbits have sizes `6` (the axes), `8` (the cube diagonals), `12` (the edge directions) and `24` (all other points), by the classification of stabilizers (a point is fixed by a nontrivial rotation iff it lies on its axis); the six-axis menu is the smallest nontrivial covariant menu.
+- M4 (seed-generated alphabet): under the unsoldered reading with finite supports, on every window formed so that each record after the first sees exactly one recorded neighbour (isolated trees under seeded growth; the ends of rows), every record lies in `{s_0, −s_0}` with `s_0` the seed's uniformly random value: a two-valued field on a random axis; with frame-attached supports the alphabet after `n` records lies in the orbit of the seeds under compositions of the frame maps.
+- M5 (Born on the antipodal menu): the overlap `(1 + s·q)/2` takes the values `1` and `0` on `{q, −q}`: on the minimal neighbour-generated menu the Born form is deterministic copying, so a nontrivial Born statistic needs a support beyond the antipodal one.
+- The clause reading: soldered ⇒ the menu is a supplied choice among unions of the four orbit types; unsoldered ⇒ the menu is generated by the recorded neighbours from a uniformly random seed. Recorded, not adopted.
+
+**Lens pass (self-run panel).**
+- *"Orbit sizes 6, 8, 12 are on `main` already."* In the barycenter-selector note as a remark; the classification here is the full statement with the stabilizer proof and the 24-point generic orbit, executed.
+- *"M2 says nothing."* It says exactly that: beyond one recorded neighbour the unsoldered reading constrains supports only through equivariance, and in particular admits no site-independent finite menu — the campaign's expected finding, now proved.
+- *"Is any of this physics?"* It fixes what the record alphabet can be under each reading: a supplied cubic orbit (soldered) or a seed-generated set (unsoldered); the six-axis menu of blocks 01–17 is the minimal soldered choice.
+
+**Forbidden phrases (beyond the lane's standing list):** "the physical menu", "selects the menu", "converge", "emergent", "certified".
+
+**Prior-art search at `origin/main`.** `git grep -n -iE "covariant support|SO\(2\)_q|antipodal menu|\{q, ?-q\}|neighbour-generated"` → the barycenter-selector note (orbit sizes as a remark), Born notes ("antipodal menu" as a supplied menu); the landed possibility-covariance note (invariants, the uniform seed law, a normalized-menu comparison with supplied probabilities); no support classification. Open PRs: none on this row.
